title: 'statement-store: reject statements without topics'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    The statement store rejects a statement without topics on submit from every source: the
    network, an RPC client and the runtime. The result is `SubmitResult::Invalid` with the new
    `InvalidReason::NoTopics`, which has the metrics label `no_topics` and the RPC reason
    `noTopics`. Such a statement was treated as a broadcast and went to every peer whatever
    filter the peer advertised.

    The affinity filter matches a statement only by its topics. A statement without topics that a
    store already holds stays there until it expires or the account quota evicts it.
crates:
- name: sp-statement-store
  bump: major
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: patch
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
